Extend `hasKind` to iterate over all own enumerable properties that are objects or arrays, rather than hard-coding field names:
```typescript
function hasKind(node: unknown, target: string): boolean {
  if (node === null || typeof node !== 'object') return false;
  if (Array.isArray(node)) return node.some(child => hasKind(child, target));
  const n = node as Record<string, unknown>;
  if (n['kind'] === target) return true;
  return Object.values(n).some(v => hasKind(v, target));
}
```
This is safe because AST nodes are plain data objects with no circular references.

